  "_comment": "CAPTURED from the live GitHub API on 2026-09-02 with a read-only GitHub App installation token (actions:read, contents:read, metadata:read, administration:read; NO packages permission), against unified-systems-com/tap. Verbatim apart from ordering, `per_page` caps, and the package owner/repository sub-objects trimmed to their identifying keys. Everything here is public. `releases_graphql` is the `repository.releases` connection of the config-layer query; `artifacts` is GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/artifacts?per_page=3 (3,636 total at capture); `packages_list_container_refused` is what GET /orgs/{org}/packages?package_type=container answers an App installation token (the OpenAPI description marks the packages endpoints enabledForGitHubApps: false); `packages_list_npm` is the 200 [] the same credential gets for a type the org has none of, which proves nothing; `package_detail` / `package_versions` are the per-package endpoints, which DID answer for a public package; the versions are the four newest (cosign signature/attestation digests, tagged `sha256-...` or untagged) plus the newest ones carrying a `sha-<short>` commit tag and `latest`, from one page of 100. Re-capture rather than hand-edit.",
